# WARP-8: the kit's ARP page is its Weave. A white key weaves the kit's pattern with another of its own (a black key
# 1-3: the kit, the sample track, the slice track to weave in), KNOB 3 the rule. PLAYS "always", or "FX + 16": the
# weave held as a throw, FX held and the last white key
wait 300
listen
expect trk 1
# P1: four kicks; P2: three snares
tapkey b0
tapkey w0
tapkey w4
tapkey w8
tapkey w12
turn PRESET 1
wait 60
tapkey b1
tapkey w2
tapkey w6
tapkey w10
turn PRESET -1
wait 60
expect drumhits 2
# ARP: the Weave page, alone; white key 2: P1 woven with P2 by bars (a bar of P1, then a bar of P2)
tap ARP
wait 40
expect page Weave
tapkey w1
wait 40
said WEAVES
shot kitweave.png
# two bars woven: 4 kicks, then 3 snares
tap PLAY
wait 3900
tap PLAY
expect drumhits 9
# PLAYS: FX + 16; now two bars plain: 8 kicks
turn K4 1
wait 40
tap PLAY
wait 3900
tap PLAY
expect drumhits 17
# held as a throw: woven again
press FX
key w15 down
wait 60
expect page Throws
said WEAVE
tap PLAY
wait 3900
tap PLAY
key w15 up
release FX
wait 40
expect drumhits 24
expect page Weave
